hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15514","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi informed us, from his father, or from his uncle, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the expedition of Tabuk: If the plague falls in a land while you are in it, then do not go out of it, and if it falls while you are not in it, then do not come upon it."
"15515","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ikrimah, meaning Ibn Khalid, from his father, or from his uncle, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the expedition of Tabuk: If the plague falls in a land while you are in it, then do not go out of it, and if it is in a land while you are not in it, then do not approach it."
